   "source": [
    "# Machine learning : Learning patterns from the data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "3ceed2d1-dc80-4324-aa15-da4652404dfb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Data Encoding : Converts the string Data into numerical data\n",
    "-> Nominal /OHE\n",
    "-> Label and ordinal \n",
    "-> Target guided ordinal encodig\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e7d0470a-18b7-4300-a222-655112ea33e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Nominal / OHE\n",
    "-> Converts Categorical Data to Numerical data\n",
    "-> No order in the data\n",
    "\n",
    "# Nominal Data Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. What is Nominal Data?\n",
    "Nominal data is categorical data with no order or ranking.\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "- Colors: Red, Blue, Green\n",
    "- Cities: Pune, Mumbai, Delhi\n",
    "- Gender: Male, Female\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Why Encoding is Required?\n",
    "Machine Learning models cannot understand text data.\n",
    "So we convert categories into numerical form.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Encoding Techniques\n",
    "\n",
    "### One-Hot Encoding (Recommended)\n",
    "- Creates separate columns for each category\n",
    "- Uses 0 and 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Color | Red | Blue | Green |\n",
    "|-------|-----|------|-------|\n",
    "| Red   | 1   | 0    | 0     |\n",
    "| Blue  | 0   | 1    | 0     |\n",
    "\n",
    "Advantages:\n",
    "- No order assumption\n",
    "- Works well with ML models\n",
    "\n",
    "Disadvantages:\n",
    "- Creates many columns\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Label Encoding (Not Recommended)\n",
    "- Assigns numbers to categories\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "Red = 0, Blue = 1, Green = 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Problem:\n",
    "- Introduces false order\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Binary Encoding\n",
    "- Combines label encoding and binary conversion\n",
    "- Reduces number of columns\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. When to Use\n",
    "\n",
    "- Few categories → One-Hot Encoding\n",
    "- Many categories → Binary Encoding\n",
    "- Ordered data → Label Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Key Points\n",
    "\n",
    "- Nominal data has no order\n",
    "- One-hot encoding is best\n",
    "- Label encoding should be avoided for nominal dataS\n"
   ]
  },
