  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "9bd7d55a-c5e8-4677-bb7e-da6a227dc49c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Label and Ordinal encoding\n",
    "    -> Label encoding -> Assigns Numerical data to each Category\n",
    "# Label Encoding vs Ordinal Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Label Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Label Encoding converts categories into numerical values.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "Red = 0  \n",
    "Blue = 1  \n",
    "Green = 2  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Points:\n",
    "- Assigns unique number to each category\n",
    "- No actual meaning of order (but model may assume order)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages:\n",
    "- Simple and fast\n",
    "- Uses only one column\n",
    "\n",
    "### Disadvantages:\n",
    "- Creates false order (0 < 1 < 2)\n",
    "- Not suitable for nominal data\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Ordinal Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Ordinal Encoding is used when categories have a meaningful order.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "Low = 1  \n",
    "Medium = 2  \n",
    "High = 3  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Points:\n",
    "- Order of categories is important\n",
    "- Numbers reflect ranking\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages:\n",
    "- Preserves order information\n",
    "- Useful for ordered data\n",
    "\n",
    "### Disadvantages:\n",
    "- Not suitable if no real order exists\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Difference Between Label and Ordinal Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature            | Label Encoding        | Ordinal Encoding       |\n",
    "|------------------|---------------------|------------------------|\n",
    "| Order matters     | No                  | Yes                    |\n",
    "| Used for          | Nominal data        | Ordinal data           |\n",
    "| Risk              | False ordering      | Misuse if no order     |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "- Use Label Encoding only when model can handle it\n",
    "- Use Ordinal Encoding when order is meaningful\n",
    "- Avoid using Label Encoding for purely nominal data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3619960a-660f-4113-a744-01732861724a",
