  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "237d5a39-497d-4f1b-9f02-af55b49eee42",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Target Guided Ordinal Encoding\n",
    "    -> Based on their relationship with the target variable\n",
    "    -> Use ful when we have large number of unique categories in categorical Value\n",
    "    -> Categorical Groups with mean/median of corresponding target variable\n",
    "\n",
    "# Target Guided Ordinal Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. What is Target Guided Ordinal Encoding?\n",
    "\n",
    "Target Guided Ordinal Encoding is a technique where categories are encoded \n",
    "based on the relationship with the target variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Categories are ordered using the mean (or probability) of the target variable\n",
    "- Higher target mean → higher rank\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Why Use It?\n",
    "\n",
    "- Captures relationship between feature and target\n",
    "- More informative than one-hot encoding\n",
    "- Reduces dimensionality\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. How It Works\n",
    "\n",
    "Steps:\n",
    "1. Group data by category\n",
    "2. Calculate mean of target variable for each category\n",
    "3. Sort categories based on mean\n",
    "4. Assign ranks (0, 1, 2, ...)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Example\n",
    "\n",
    "| City   | Purchased (Target) |\n",
    "|--------|-------------------|\n",
    "| Pune   | 1                 |\n",
    "| Mumbai | 0                 |\n",
    "| Pune   | 1                 |\n",
    "| Delhi  | 0                 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Mean Target:\n",
    "- Pune → 1.0\n",
    "- Mumbai → 0.0\n",
    "- Delhi → 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "Encoding:\n",
    "- Mumbai → 0\n",
    "- Delhi → 1\n",
    "- Pune → 2\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "- Uses target information\n",
    "- Improves model performance\n",
    "- Handles high cardinality well\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. Disadvantages\n",
    "\n",
    "- Risk of overfitting\n",
    "- Data leakage if not applied carefully\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. Key Points\n",
    "\n",
    "- Also called Mean Encoding (simplified version)\n",
    "- Always apply on training data only\n",
    "- Use with cross-validation for safety"
   ]
  },
